{
  "title": "Creature growth on twelve consecutive body plans",
  "reproduce": "In character-view/creature-plan.js, call buildCreature(randomCreaturePlan(seed)). Export through character-view/export-form.js exportForm(form,{motion:true,game:true,atlasSize:1024}). For the matched control use the same random plan with back replaced by the recorded previousBack. Before export, all twelve control forms were checked for exact equality with their saved pre-change versions.",
  "steering": "In Creature body plan, open Along the back. Select shingles, gill fans, drum sacs or shag mantle. Count, height and spread change geometry. Reroll growth changes the local pattern. An agent can send steerCreature with set.back. Individual shingle sites can still be edited or tip-locked.",
  "evidence": {
    "paired": "docs/media/creature-back-growth.webp",
    "unpickedTwelve": "docs/media/creature-growth-seeds.webp",
    "renderer": "NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Ti/PCIe/SSE2",
    "export": "Production Game GLB, animated, one skinned surface, shared 1024px material atlas. A native Canvas2D adapter supplied atlas packing while running the workshop exporter in Node. PNG payloads were decoded from the GLBs.",
    "raster": "Native OpenGL rasterization of outward-facing exported triangles at rest. Colors sample the exported atlas and vertex colors under fixed diffuse lighting; 2x supersampling. Each control and candidate use shared bounds, pixel scale and lighting per view. The twelve-draw sheet fits each creature to its cell and prints the actual world height.",
    "measurementCamera": "365 x 300 pixels. Three fixed azimuth/elevation pairs [22,12], [106,10], [167,23] degrees. Count an exported growth region with at least 12 visible pixels using the GLB _REGION attribute. IoU is the intersection over union of control and candidate silhouette masks at that view.",
    "exampleDetail": "The third column uses a tighter camera fitted to the new organs on the same exported model.",
